---
// component imports
import MainLayout from "../../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import type { ComponentProps } from "astro/types";
import reveal from "./reveal.astro";
---

<MainLayout title="Code Fun">
  <section class="post">
    <h1 class="page-title heading">CODING FUN</h1>
    <h2 class="page-title">
      <a href="https://weirdweboctober.website/" target="_blank">Weird Web October</a>
    </h2>
    <div class="page-container">
      <h3>Day 1: <a href="/projects/code-fun/reveal">Reveal</a></h3>
      <ul>
        <li>I combined 3 different october challenge prompts this year: Reveal, Oak, and Cozy Coffee!</li>
        <li>Used GSAP Draggable for the dragging functionality.</li>
        <li>Due to how Safari handles its viewport and fixed positioning differently than other browsers, I decided to fix the scroll to the body, hence why the leaves don't move as you scroll. This way, I can ensure at least the leaves are covering the drawing initially in all browswers. Not ideal, but it's the best I got.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</MainLayout>
<style>
  img {
    max-width: 400px;
    max-height: 400px;
    width: auto;
    height: auto;
  }

  #carouselTargetList {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    grid-gap: 1rem;
    justify-content: center;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .page-title {
    text-align: center;
  }
  li {
    display: inline-block;
    list-style-type: none;
  }
  .page-container {
    display: flex;
    grid-gap: 1rem;
    justify-content: center;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .page-grid {
    visibility: hidden;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    width: 300px;
  }
  @media screen and (max-width: 340px) {
    img {
      max-width: 200px;
      max-height: 200px;
    }
  }
  @media screen and (max-width: 640px) {
    .page-container {
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
    .heading {
      font-size: 40px;
    }
  }
</style>
<script>
